TITLE='Authentic title "Why Everything Changes After You Start Looking Poor" reuses the channel\'s "Why Everything Changes After..." threshold frame. The script delivers stealth-wealth (Stanley-Danko, lifestyle creep, lottery-neighbour bankruptcies, redirecting car payments), then flips to the poverty premium (payday, subprime, insurance) and quiet luxury. It answers the title in both directions. TYPICAL against the cohort. Association only.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White background. Left: the recurring cartoon man in a torn, patched grey T-shirt and patched jeans with a smug half-smile. Right: a heavy black two-line headline "THE POOR STRATEGY" above a padlocked green safe, with a curved arrow pointing at the safe. At 320x180 the headline, ragged figure and locked safe stay legible. The visual matches the "looking poor while secretly wealthy" thesis, and the safe signals hidden wealth.'
SCRIPT='A single-narrator essay with composites: red-light hook (leased sedan vs old Camry); channel pitch and an open loop on the lottery study; Stanley-Danko millionaire habits; Experian luxury-car ownership; Goldman paycheck-to-paycheck at $300-500K; Diderot effect and hedonic adaptation; car payments, 84-month loans, negative equity; dealer payment framing; BNPL for burritos, Coachella and groceries; Fed lottery-neighbour bankruptcy study; redirected $700 payment to ~$850K; savings rate and early start; Buffett and Kamprad; paid community plug; poverty premium (payday, subprime, rent-to-own, insurance); Veblen; dress-based service; underconsumption, loud budgeting, money dysmorphia; quiet luxury; objection about appearances; close and community plug. Reproduces: $700 x 30 years at 7%/8%; 30-vs-35-year gap. Mostly accurate references. Caveats: Toyota statistic from a later Stanley book; Experian figures dated; auto figures slightly behind the latest Edmunds quarter; rent-to-own example exceeds the stated multiple. The stored ending is complete.'
BEATS=['Hook: Peter\'s leased sedan vs Lara\'s Camry.','Thesis and channel pitch; lottery open loop.','Stanley-Danko millionaire habits.','Experian luxury-car data; Goldman 41%.','Diderot effect.','Hedonic adaptation.','Car payments and negative equity.','Dealer payment framing.','BNPL: burritos, Coachella, groceries.','Lottery-neighbour bankruptcy study.','Redirected $700 payment.','Savings rate; early start; 30 vs 35.','Buffett and Kamprad.','Community plug.','Poverty premium: payday, subprime, rent-to-own.','Insurance by credit and ZIP; Veblen.','Dress-based treatment.','Underconsumption, loud budgeting, money dysmorphia.','Quiet luxury.','Objection: appearances in sales jobs.','Permission to look like less; close and plug.']
